<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Xanten</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1614</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-julich-succession">War of the Jülich Succession</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Xanten was signed on 12 November 1614 to settle the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-julich-succession">War of the Jülich Succession</a>, which followed the death of the last duke of Jülich-Cleves-Berg in 1609. It divided the inheritance between the two main claimants: the Elector of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a> received <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kleve">Cleves</a>, Mark and Ravensberg, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/count-palatine">Count Palatine</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neuburg-an-der-donau">Neuburg</a> received Jülich and Berg. It gave the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-hohenzollern">Hohenzollerns</a> their first territories in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>.</p></div>
